{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested for S1 exact 0d1c7e11a3989bdfbaffeb60729be120821fdf86 and primary git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:8d6e6b67775c435351ff13dd4666430654b71bb7. Governing child git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:ac54fe712abc7ca0614ca1067bad1a7ff8c490b0, implementation promise git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:a4c569b1cddfb0db72f9239488851f19a291906f, ordinary adopted proposal git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:7a71886b58aae707adfad0e1f4f98e6f464c6577 ratified by Hugh in git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:ba18cd1a375156c663cea2bc7e1062b1ac3839b8. I read the full review request, primary report, adopted proposal, all three durable stage requests, production changes and contract notes, and examined the relevant fixtures. Ordinary inherited staleness is acknowledged. This is a bounded defect review, not approval of the remaining proof obligations.\n\nRequired corrections, reproduced against this exact head with Go 1.26.7 and real Git in disposable fixtures:\n\n1. Include the captured checkout inputs in association cache validity, or cache only the ref-derived portion and rebuild checkout membership/heads per call. Associations caches rows containing Checkouts and detached heads under only frontier plus refs. My TestCodexAssociationCacheIncludesDetachedInputs creates two real unreferenced commit-tree heads A and B with the same request trailer, captures one Snapshot, calls Associations with detached A, then calls with detached B at the same refs/frontier. The cold positive is complete and claimed. The second call incorrectly returns A's cached row, omits B and leaves B's grade blank. A detached checkout can move or a checkout can be added, removed or renamed without changing a ref or a durable record; this answer can remain wrong indefinitely. Retain existing ref move/rename invalidation and clone returned cache data fully.\n\n2